📓 JournalApp
  JournalApp is a Java-based web application built with Spring Boot that allows users to create, view, update, and delete personal journal entries using secure REST APIs. This project focuses on clean architecture, secure data handling, and modern development practices — perfect for learning and real-world application development.

🔥 Key Features
•	Secure login & authentication using Spring Security.
•	CRUD operations for journal entries via RESTful APIs.
•	MongoDB as the NoSQL database -> Connection using Mongo Atlas.
•	Clean code structure with Spring Data MongoDB and JPA.
•	Unit testing with JUnit5 and Mockito.
•	Logging with Slf4j using (Logback, JUL, Log4j2 ).
•	API tested with Postman.

⚙️ Tech Stack
•	Java ---> Backend Programming Language  
•	Spring Boot ---> Application Framework
•	Rest APIs ---> Application Communication
•	Postman ---> API Testing Tool MongoDB
•	Spring Security ---> Authentication & Authorization
•	Maven ---> Build and Dependency Management  
•	MongoDB ---> NoSQL Database
•	Spring Data MongoDB ---> ORM abstraction for MongoDB
•	JUnit5 & Mockito ---> Enhanced Unit Testing Frameworks
•	Logging ---> Abstract layer Slf4j => Logback, log4j2, Java Util logging (JUL).

